# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Security + cache headers for the STATIC pages (Cloudflare Pages).
# Spec: docs/architecture/backlog/live-sim-demo.md §4.7. `_headers` does NOT apply to
# Pages *Function* responses (settled by a real deploy) — /api/* headers live in
# functions/api/_lib/envelope.js. Later rules win, so cache rules are ordered below.
#
# CSP, directive by directive:
#  · connect-src 'self' is the strongest control: no script can ship data off-site (it
#    has a measured kill — it refused the port-8081 fetch). Widened by exactly one host,
#    challenges.cloudflare.com, for Turnstile telemetry. sim/test_csp.mjs proves an
#    arbitrary off-origin fetch is still refused.
#  · script-src has no 'unsafe-inline': every inline block became a file except sim.html's
#    importmap (importmaps cannot be external; sim.html needs it because the vendored
#    three.js addons import bare "three"). Its hash is GENERATED by
#    sim/tools/build_csp_hashes.py (never typed; --check runs in CI) — a drifted hash
#    blanks the page in production. No inline handler attributes exist either;
#    `el.onclick = fn` is a DOM property write, which CSP does not police.
#  · static.cloudflareinsights.com: Pages INJECTS its analytics beacon into every HTML
#    response. Refusing it logs a CSP error on every production load. Its reports go
#    same-origin (/cdn-cgi/rum), so connect-src needs nothing. DO NOT tidy this away —
#    the tag is not in this repo, so nothing local breaks when it goes.
#  · challenges.cloudflare.com in script-src, frame-src and connect-src: the Turnstile
#    widget (sim/web/turnstile.js) must be served from that host, renders in its iframe,
#    and each missing directive fails SILENTLY (no token). Host-exact: never widen to
#    cloudflare.com "for symmetry". The sitekey arrives at runtime from /api/health, never
#    from this repo.
#  · style-src keeps 'unsafe-inline' ONLY for docs.html's Mermaid, which emits per-diagram
#    runtime <style> + style= attributes (no hash can cover them; strict CSP draws the
#    diagrams unstyled). CSSOM writes (el.style.x = …) are not policed and are not a
#    reason. test_csp.mjs block 10 is an INVERTING guard: the day Mermaid stops needing
#    this it reddens, and the fix is to delete 'unsafe-inline' here. A per-path CSP was
#    rejected: Pages' merge semantics for two matching CSP rules are unverified and the
#    hash generator rewrites only the first CSP line.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: microphone=(self), camera=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-6RkvnLhc+Dxs3DRMSy+Rs0us73msKNskVUvxIBn7gdw=' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com; img-src 'self' data: blob:; media-src 'self' data: blob:; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'none'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'

# HTML — always revalidate so a redeploy's new asset references show up immediately.
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# App scripts must revalidate. THE LIST IS THE WHOLE MECHANISM (the /*.js glob is
# unreliable on Pages): an unlisted script gets default caching, so a redeploy can leave a
# visitor running yesterday's file against today's HTML. sim/test_csp.mjs enumerates
# sim/web/*.js (and each script subdirectory's rule) and fails on any omission.
/moxie.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/diagram.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/ambient.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/mic.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/stub.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/qr.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/bg.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/moxie-wire.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/env.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/mode.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/life.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/cloud-transport.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/sw-reset.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/hud.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/rail.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/home.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/setup.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/cloud.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/docs.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/wire-bg.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/turnstile.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/moxie/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/bridge/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/voice/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/css/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Rendered imagery + docs bundle — short cache so overwrites propagate fast.
/img/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
/docs-bundle/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
/ambient.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/docs-index.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/docs-search.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/fixtures/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
/sessions/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
/audio/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# Vendored libraries + fonts — content-addressed, safe to cache for a year.
# (Listed AFTER the no-cache rules so it wins for vendored .js. The /api/* block below
#  sets no Cache-Control for these paths, so it cannot disturb that.)
/vendor/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# /api/* (Pages Functions): INERT here — see the header note. Kept as documentation of
# intent; test_demo_proxy.mjs holds it in agreement with envelope.js, where the real
# headers are set.
/api/*
  Cache-Control: no-store
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: same-origin
